  "segments": [
    {
      "t0Ms": 15893,
      "t1Ms": 43555,
      "text": "I kept a map of every wrong turn Folded thin from overuse Held it up against the evening Like proof I could not choose Then the street lights came in slow"
    },
    {
      "t0Ms": 46302,
      "t1Ms": 73913,
      "text": "And took the edges off the view In ruins of unfinished life I learned to name what I can't keep Not every ache needs to be right Some truths arrive when I let them sleep"
    },
    {
      "t0Ms": 76610,
      "t1Ms": 105098,
      "text": "I used to chase the perfect timing Count each breath before I spoke Now I leave a little silence For the words that still have hope If morning finds me half-assemble"
    },
    {
      "t0Ms": 107390,
      "t1Ms": 134865,
      "text": "That will still be more than none I am not the sum of tremors I am also what I've done In rooms of unfinished life I learned to name what I can keep"
    },
    {
      "t0Ms": 137174,
      "t1Ms": 161764,
      "text": "Not every ache needs to be mine Some truths arrive when I let them sleep"
    },
